  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 105 AM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nAn upper low to our south will continue tracking eastward today. \nHigh resolution models keep precipitation south of the ID-UT border \nwith only very slight chances for showers across the extreme \nsouthern extent of Idaho.\n\nA weak shortwave will swing through the state on Thursday, bringing \nlow-end chances for precipitation across the higher terrain Thursday \nevening through early Friday. High resolution models feature some \nvery light precipitation across the central and eastern mountains \nwith National Blend PoPs up to around 25 percent.\n\nDaytime temperatures will remain very stable through late week with \nwidespread highs ranging the 40s. As weak high pressure takes hold \nagain, southwest flow will warm temperatures by 5 to 10 degrees on \nSunday. Temperatures will run about 5 degrees above climatological \nnorms early next week, ranging the 50s for much of Southeast\nIdaho.",
